  "lineage": "English Protestant hymn tradition codified through the 6,500+ hymn texts of Charles Wesley (1707-1788) and the canonical Methodist hymn-book A Collection of Hymns for the use of the People called Methodists (1780, John Wesley editor). The Methodist tradition emphasizes intensely personal-devotional content (the \"warmed heart\" theme), strong congregational singing as central liturgical practice, and the use of vernacular-popular-tune adaptations alongside specifically-composed Methodist hymn-tunes. Major influence on the broader English-speaking-world Protestant hymnody.",
